    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nWhen an owner is created without a `registrationDate`, it now defaults to the server's current date; a supplied date is preserved. The value is stored and returned as an ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` string.\n\n## Changes (kept as small, low-coupling units)\n\n1. **`OwnerRegistrationDateAdvice`** (new) \u2014 a tiny `RequestBodyAdviceAdapter` that sets `registrationDate = LocalDate.now()` on the incoming `OwnerFieldsDto` only when it's null. This mirrors the existing `OwnerEmailNormalizationAdvice` pattern, so the default-date rule lives in its own cohesive class instead of growing the controller (which has high surrounding complexity).\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added a persisted `registrationDate` field (`@Column(name = \"registration_date\")`) plus its getter/setter and the `LocalDate` import. This is the only edit to an existing class, and just adds simple accessors.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `registrationDate` (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so the generated DTO both accepts it on `POST` and echoes it on `GET`. MapStruct maps it by name automatically, so the mapper needed no changes.\n\n4. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql` / `data.sql`** \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column and extended the positional seed inserts to match. hsqldb is the test database (`ddl-auto=none`); the main-app h2 profile uses `ddl-auto=update`, which adds the column automatically after script init, so those files didn't need touching.\n\nThe default logic and the mapping flow through fresh/low-complexity units, and no existing method's body was grown \u2014 only accessors were added.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest` (both `coreDefaultsToToday` and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate`) and the full `mvn test` suite pass \u2014 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
